    "wacc_rationale": "The rate is a COST OF EQUITY, not a WACC: the capitalised flow (AFFO) is already after interest. USD basis: ~4.3% 10-year US Treasury assumption + ~0.8 beta x 5% ERP = ~8.0-8.5%; base 8.0%, bull 7.5%, bear 9.0%. The risk-free input is an assumption, not a fetched quote.",
    "lease_treatment": "Ground-lease cost is already inside property operating expenses and therefore inside Normalized FFO; no separate lease path and no lease liability deducted.",
    "nci_treatment": "Normalized FFO is stated attributable to common stockholders (NCI share of depreciation and normalising items already removed). OP units (3.25m) are counted in the share base rather than as a deduction.",
    "notes": "MODEL: REIT AFFO capitalisation at cost of equity, run through the Drivers engine with net debt held at zero. Reason: Ventas is a healthcare REIT (SHOP senior housing, outpatient medical & research, triple-net); FFO/AFFO is post-interest, so capitalising it at a WACC or deducting the $12.4bn of debt afterwards would count the debt twice. Reported debt and cash are recorded as reported_total_debt / reported_cash for audit only. AFFO IS DERIVED, NOT DISCLOSED: Ventas reports only Nareit FFO and Normalized FFO. Base AFFO = Q3-2026 Normalized FFO 514.227 x 4 = 2,056.9 (NEW definition, which from Q1-2026 adds back non-cash SBC) less TTM SBC 42.4 (re-deducted, so the definition change is neutralised) less maintenance capex 450 (9M-2026 'Other capital expenditures' 319.3 annualised to 426 and rounded up for Q4 seasonality; treated as 100% recurring because the 10-Q does not split FAD capex -- conservative) less straight-line rent ~34 (9M 25.4 annualised) = ~1,531, or ~$2.87 per fully diluted share. Redevelopment/development spend (214.3 in 9M-2026) is growth capex and is not deducted; the growth path is correspondingly limited to same-store/organic growth. ENGINE MAPPING: base_revenue = Q3-2026 revenue 1,831.8 x 4; ebitda_margin_path = pre-SBC AFFO margin (21.47%); sbc_pct_path = SBC % of revenue; D&A, capex, tax and working capital are zero because they are already inside AFFO. growth_rates are AFFO-per-existing-share growth, NOT reported revenue growth: reported revenue will grow faster through acquisitions funded by new equity, which this model treats as value-neutral. Normalized FFO figures for 2025 and earlier in the Metrics CSV are on the OLD (post-SBC) basis and are not comparable with 2026 quarters without adding SBC back. No FY2026 guidance paragraph is carried in the 10-Q text (guidance is in the 8-K earnings release, not in Extracted/), so year-1 growth is judged from the Q3-2026 same-store prints, not from guidance. Entry-price hurdle of 15% is the house hurdle and is very demanding for a REIT; read the entry price as a deep-value marker.",
